   "speech": "Ranum sighed deeply. The passer-by’s soul, perfectly plain to him, was dead, as a clock is dead. Its mechanical functions worked admirably, as was witnessed by the passer-by’s lively, keen glance and by his being overburdened with cares for his family and his bread; but the magical principle of the soul, the divine light of the Great Power, had gone out. A rose that has lost its fragrance might serve as the symbol of this state. The passer-by’s soul had been killed by years of shocks, by the poison of evil impressions. The epoch abounded in them. Their unbroken series, in a crude scheme, may be expressed thus: anguish, oppression, violence, blood, death, corpses, despair. The spirit, shuddering, had glutted itself on them, had grown coarse and died; it had become a corpse to all the agitation of life. Even so a plank flung into a whirlpool of waves, amid the manifold seething of the waters’ forces, invariably keeps the flatness of its surface, moving lifelessly hither and thither.",
